==Swedish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|sv|non|eptir}}, from {{inh|sv|gem-pro|*aftiri||more aft, further behind}}, {{m|gem-pro|*after}}, from {{inh|sv|ine-pro|*apotero||further behind, further away}}, comparative form of {{m|ine-pro|*apo-||off, behind}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|sv|/ˈɛftɛr/}}
* {{audio|sv|Sv-efter.ogg|audio (Gotland)}}
* {{rhymes|sv|¹ɛftɛr|s=2}}

===Adverb===
{{sv-adv|mermest}}

# [[after]]

===Adjective===
{{sv-adj|-}}

# {{lb|sv|only used predicatively}} [[slow]] (from notion of behind others)
#: {{ux|sv|Han är lite '''efter'''|He is a bit '''slow'''}}

===Preposition===
{{head|sv|preposition}}

# [[after]]; subsequent; later in time than ''or'' later in a sequence than
# [[by]]; using the rules or logic of
# [[by]]; ''as in'' one by one, one after another
#: {{ux|sv|en '''efter''' en|one '''by''' one}}
# [[by]]; in a manner conforming or corresponding to
#: {{ux|sv|Sortera dem '''efter''' storlek och färg|Sort them '''by''' size and color}}

